What:		/sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/enabled
Date:		October 2026
Description:	Runtime boolean switch for CONFIG_KSHRINK_SLABD, when built
		in; defaults to false. Disabling rejects new asynchronous
		requests under the request lock and waits for pending/running
		work and its memcg reference release. Global scan cancels
		pending work and interrupts running iteration at the next
		group boundary; an active shrinker must return first. A successful write of
		false guarantees idle background reclaim on return. The wait
		is freezable and may be interrupted by a signal: on error,
		admission stays disabled but drain is not guaranteed; write
		false again to retry. Invalid input does not change state.
		Freezing can defer completion until thaw; no bounded latency
		is promised. Direct reclaim, drop_caches, severe pressure and
		a busy/unavailable worker remain synchronous. The Kconfig
		option is also off in the default configuration.

What:		/sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/global_scan
Date:		November 2026
Description:	Boolean mode, default false (single-request mode). True
		selects one serial all-memcg scan on an accepted root/global
		kswapd request. Only the accepted call skips synchronous
		reclaim; nonroot, busy, direct and severe-pressure calls do
		not. Change requires admission disabled and pending/running
		work drained; otherwise EBUSY, including repeated writes.
		Invalid input leaves mode unchanged. Shares the existing
		worker and slot. Optional policy below supplies adaptive deadlines.

What:           /sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/policy
Date:           November 2026
Description:    Boolean adaptive global policy, default false. Change only
                disabled/idle (otherwise EBUSY). Effective only with global_scan
                and enabled. Uses the existing worker deadline and request slot.
                An enabled transition starts at max_sleep_time. No new root
                after a scan means deadline recalculation only, without scan.

What:           /sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/app_launch_scenario
Date:           November 2026
Description:    Administrator 0/1 input; global policy must be enabled, otherwise
                EINVAL. Starts one 3000 ms session; repeated 1 does not extend
                it. 0, expiry or disable ends once. Policy requests may skip;
                accepted transfers remain fulfilled and new transfers stay
                synchronous during launch. No automatic ROM writer is claimed.

What:           /sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/sleep_time
What:           /sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/max_sleep_time
What:           /sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/priority
What:           /sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/slab_pressure_high_mb
What:           /sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/slab_pressure_low_mb
Date:           November 2026
Description:    Unsigned controls: sleep_time 1000..30000 ms (future interval),
                max_sleep_time 1000..120000 ms, priority 0..12, high <=2048 MiB
                and >low, low >=50 MiB and <high. Invalid input returns EINVAL
                without changing state. Default high/low use RAM rounding,
                documented in Documentation/vm/kshrink_slabd.rst. Pending
                priority is never raised by a control write. Delays are bounded
                by max_sleep_time, including a user-written sleep_time.

What:           /sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/stats
Date:           November 2026
Description:    Read-only cumulative transferred/fallback/hints/periodic,
                recalculations/scans/objects/skips, force_wakes and launch
                started/ended counters, plus pending/busy/iterator/launch/timer,
                current sleep_ms and capped backoff. objects are shrink_slab
                returned objects, not pages or bytes. scans are attempted
                policy-active scan rounds (may abort under pressure). After
                successful disable pending/busy/iterator/launch/timer are zero
                and periodic/scans/objects/launch counts stop growing until
                enable; synchronous fallback counts may still grow.
